Presentation rows (plan P3-23): a class of the document's shows as its own element, with an ARIA role and a frame the theme draws; a role reads as an inline element; the host turns quotes into asides.

#{
  $.counter('thm')
  $.element('theorem', {
    counter: 'thm', numbering: 'always', supplement: {en: 'Theorem '},
    sites: [{where: 'prepend', at: 'first-para', template: [strong(slot('supplement'), slot('number'), '.'), ' ']}],
    html: {element: 'section', aria: 'note', typeset: {frame: true, dataRole: true}},
  })
  $.element('key', {html: {element: 'kbd', inline: true}})
}

#!theorem(label: "t1")
Every presentation row is data.
#theorem!

Press #strong({role: 'key'})[Ctrl] to copy; see @t1.

> A quote the host shows as an aside.
